1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,400
The Great Wall of China.

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:11,025
The Great Wall is not a single continuous structure but a series of fortifications built over 2,000 years by successive Chinese dynasties.

3
00:00:11,025 --> 00:00:20,800
The earliest sections date to the 7th century BCE; the most visited sections were constructed during the Ming Dynasty (1368-1644).

4
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:29,337
The total network spans over 21,000 kilometers, though contrary to popular belief, it is not visible from space with the naked eye.

5
00:00:29,337 --> 00:00:34,787
Millions of laborers, including soldiers and prisoners, worked on its construction.

6
00:00:34,787 --> 00:00:42,125
The Wall never functioned as an impenetrable barrier; its primary role was regulating trade and controlling border crossings.

7
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:45,225
It is a UNESCO World Heritage site.

